# Prompt Principles for AI Coding Agents

A prompt is a specification: every token load-bearing, the minimum explicit information the receiving model needs and nothing more. Verbosity is not just waste; filler buries the load-bearing tokens and degrades the receiving model's output.

## Reduction gate

Cut before sending, and never emit the draft. Keep what would force a re-ask if cut: interfaces, paths, error text, the input/output spec, the output format, hard constraints, and the one-line intent. Everything off that list is deletable.

When distilling a source (an incident report, a feedback doc, a book) into instructions, keep the directive and drop the story. No provenance (work-item IDs, dates, "learned in..."), and no slogans or branded headings; a heading states the directive itself, as in "Verify by durable state, never by exit status" rather than "The one rule:" or "Corollaries (w11):". A "why" survives only as a parenthetical of at most one clause that stops the reader from undoing the rule; history stays in the plan or log.

## Priorities

Prefer precision over politeness, directives and interface contracts over explanations, constraints over preferences, and concrete over abstract.

## Structure

| Element | When | Example |
|---------|------|---------|
| Intent upfront | Always | "Split UserService: extract NotificationService" |
| Delimiters | Distinct sections | `<context>`, `<instructions>`, `<constraints>` |
| Input/output spec | Transformations | "Input: handlers.py. Output: handlers.py, validators.py" |
| Format directive | Controlling output shape | "Output only code, no explanation" |
| Concrete example | Task-local mapping or boundary case; never a default rail in reusable context | `{"user_name": "x"}` maps to `{"userName": "x"}` |

## Context

Include interfaces, exact errors, file structure, and domain rules. Exclude history, ruled-out options, and unrelated files. The test for any piece of context: would the model hallucinate without it, or does it constrain the solution? If neither, cut it.

## Constraints

State constraints that narrow the solution space.

## Feedback

Vague feedback is the weak form; a precise defect report is the strong form. "That's not quite right" becomes "serialize() drops None; keep it as null", and "This broke something" becomes "redis is not in deps; use utils/cache.py". Never restate style rules a doc already carries; write "Follow CODING_PRINCIPLES.md".

