1685:{"id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","title":"Plan source installs and citation remaps","description":"## Given/When/Then\n**Given:** the converter candidates `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/\u003cstem\u003e/pymupdf/\u003cstem\u003e.md` and the existing original Markdown baseline for Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79 and VISOR_S-MOC_Herbicide_91234-52-89391 with `artifacts/conversion_v42/comparison.json` (`labels[stem].reference_sha256` = the live `.md` hash at conversion time) (the reference files already came from Marker; no new conversion receipt is required); the manager's localized repair proposal `artifacts/conversion_v42/localized_repairs_proposal_v2.json` (`{stem: [{line, before, after, pdf_page_0, reason}]}`) for Volunteer_66222-60-55467 and Crop_Protect_Direct_Paraquat_3SL_101458-2; the frozen judge inputs `data_runs/scratch/judge3_\u003cstem\u003e_new.json`; the salvaged Willowood candidate `data_runs/recovered_candidates_v42/Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79.v2-opus5.json` with its receipt (`candidate_sha256`); `dedup_rates_rows.py` (`row_signature`, `dedup_record`); `farmplanner/filter/label_pages.py::_page_for_line(meta_with_lines, line)` (1-based page from a caller-supplied `_md_lines`); the correction JSON shape `apply_rate_corrections.py` accepts (`stem, original_input, original_input_sha256, sources, operations, expected`, operations `{stem, field, operation, before, after, row_signature, prior_finding, pdf_page_0, source_sha256, reason}`). Live sources under `/home/ben/projects/farmplanner/data/production/labels/\u003cstem\u003e/` are read only.\n**When:** `uv run python work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py plan --version 2 --candidates-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42 --candidate-repairs work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/candidate_heading_repairs_v48.json --localized work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/localized_repairs_proposal_v2.json --labels-dir /home/ben/projects/farmplanner/data/production/labels --inputs-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/scratch --recovered-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/recovered_candidates_v42 --out-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42` runs.\n**Then:** for every candidate of every install stem, and for every localized proposal, a deterministic citation remap in the correction-JSON shape exists beside a plan receipt, with unresolved rows listed and never guessed, so the source-comparison review can check the remaps together with the candidates before anything is installed. No live file changes.\n\n## Touches\n- `tests/test_source_text.py`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/source_text.py`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/source_remap.py`\n- `CODEMAP.md`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py`\n- `tests/test_install_label_sources.py`\n- `codemap/testing.md`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42/**`\n\n## Contract\n- Dispatch precondition (manager, recorded in manager_log.md before dispatch): the run checkout was provisioned with `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/provision.sh \u003crun\u003e`, which links the gitignored frozen judge inputs `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/scratch/judge3_\u003cstem\u003e_new.json` from the item checkout, byte-checked. The builder first checks `test -f work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/scratch/judge3_VISOR_S-MOC_Herbicide_91234-52-89391_new.json` and stops with `source_plan: blocked run not provisioned` when it is absent; it never copies or regenerates the inputs.\n- `install_label_sources.py` has two subcommands, `plan` (this bead) and `apply` (run by the install bead after the review; implemented here, exercised on tmp fixtures by the tests, never with `--apply` against the live directory in this bead). Pure functions at module level (`remap_rows`, `shift_rows_for_localized`, `verify_before_lines`, receipt builders); file I/O in `main`. Import `row_signature`/`dedup_record` from `dedup_rates_rows` (work dir on `sys.path` relative to `__file__`), never copy them.\n- `plan` step 0: `mkdir -p \u003cout-dir\u003e/\u003cstem\u003e` for every stem it handles (nothing exists yet). Refuse when a candidate named in `comparison.json` is missing, or when the live `.md` hash differs from `comparison.json` `reference_sha256` for that stem (`refuse: live source changed since comparison`).\n- Input records per stem: for VISOR 91234-52 and the two localized stems, the deduplicated judge input `judge3_\u003cstem\u003e_new.json` (`dedup_record` first; a duplicate twin yields exactly one remap operation for the surviving row, and the dropped twins are listed in the plan receipt as `dedup_dropped: [{row, twin_signature}]`). Willowood had no v3 extraction, so no `judge3_Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79_new.json` exists and none is required: its only input record is the salvaged candidate `data_runs/recovered_candidates_v42/Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79.v2-opus5.json`, deduplicated the same way, whose bytes must hash to the receipt's `candidate_sha256` (else refuse `candidate hash differs from receipt`). A stem whose named input is missing refuses with `input record missing: \u003cpath\u003e`; the judge input is never substituted for Willowood.\n- Whole-replacement remap, per install stem and per candidate (`pymupdf`): for every deduplicated rate row, locate the row's text under its `source_section` heading in the candidate Markdown: find the heading (normalised match: collapse whitespace, strip `#`, casefold), then within that section the first line span containing the row's numeric amount tokens and unit words; when found emit `{stem, field: \"application_rates\", operation: \"replace\", before: \u003crow\u003e, after: \u003crow with new source_line_range\u003e, row_signature: row_signature(row), prior_finding: \"source_repair_v42\", pdf_page_0: \u003c_page_for_line(candidate_meta_with_lines, start) - 1\u003e, source_sha256: \u003ccandidate sha256\u003e, reason: \"source_line_range remapped after source replacement\"}`; when the heading or the span is ambiguous or missing, append `{row_signature, source_section, reason}` to `unresolved` instead. Never guess a range. Write `\u003cout-dir\u003e/\u003cstem\u003e/line_remap_\u003ccandidate\u003e_v1.json` in the exact correction shape (`original_input` = the judge input or the salvaged candidate path, `original_input_sha256`, `sources: [{path: \u003ccandidate path\u003e, sha256}, {path: \u003cpdf\u003e, sha256}]`, `operations`, `expected: {final_rate_rows: \u003cdeduplicated count\u003e, untouched_rate_rows: \u003cdeduplicated count minus operations\u003e, rate_dependencies: \"unchanged\", other_fields: \"unchanged\"}`) plus the extra key `unresolved` (tolerated by the apply tool).\n- Localized remap, per localized stem: `verify_before_lines` checks every `{line, before}` against the current live line (1-based, exact); a mismatch is recorded as `before_mismatch` for that stem and no remap is written for it. Otherwise compute the line shift for each proposal (`line_delta` = lines inserted minus removed at or before a row's `source_line_range` start) and emit one `replace` operation per affected deduplicated row with the shifted range (`prior_finding: \"source_repair_v42\"`, `reason: \"source_line_range shifted after localized repair\"`, `source_sha256` = hash of the repaired text computed in memory); rows with no shift get no operation. Write `\u003cout-dir\u003e/\u003cstem\u003e/line_remap_localized_v1.json` in the same shape, and `\u003cout-dir\u003e/\u003cstem\u003e/localized_preview_v1.md` (the repaired text, for the review).\n- Plan receipt `\u003cout-dir\u003e/\u003cstem\u003e/plan_v1.json`: `{stem, kind: \"replacement|localized\", candidates: {\u003ccandidate\u003e: {path, sha256, operations, unresolved}}, live_sha256, dedup_dropped, before_mismatch: [...], generated_at}`; a later `plan` run with the same inputs is byte-identical apart from `generated_at`.\n- `apply` (for the install bead): refuses unless the review JSON names a passing candidate or passing localized verdict for the stem, the chosen candidate's remap has `unresolved == []`, and the live hash still equals the plan's `live_sha256`; the install bead's description carries the full apply contract.\n- Tests `tests/test_install_label_sources.py` on tmp fixtures: `test_remap_emits_one_operation_per_deduplicated_row`, `test_ambiguous_span_is_unresolved_not_guessed`, `test_localized_before_mismatch_writes_no_remap`, `test_localized_shift_only_affects_rows_after_insertion`, `test_plan_refuses_when_live_hash_differs_from_comparison`, `test_apply_refuses_unresolved_remap`, `test_apply_replacement_restores_parked_copy_on_hash_mismatch`, `test_plan_writes_nothing_outside_out_dir`. Add one row for the new test file to `codemap/testing.md` in the same commit.\n- Final line: `source_plan: stems=\u003cn\u003e replacement_candidates=\u003cc\u003e localized=\u003cl\u003e unresolved=\u003cu\u003e before_mismatch=\u003cm\u003e`.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Run every command below from the root of the current run checkout (the builder's worktree), never a hard-coded item checkout; absolute `/home/ben/projects/farmplanner/...` paths name authorized live data only.\n- [ ] `test -f work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/scratch/judge3_VISOR_S-MOC_Herbicide_91234-52-89391_new.json \u0026\u0026 echo run_provisioned`\n- [ ] `uv run pytest tests/test_install_label_sources.py -q \u0026\u0026 grep -q 'tests/test_install_label_sources.py' codemap/testing.md`\n- [ ] `set -o pipefail; uv run python work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py plan --version 2 --candidates-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42 --candidate-repairs work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/candidate_heading_repairs_v48.json --localized work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/localized_repairs_proposal_v2.json --labels-dir /home/ben/projects/farmplanner/data/production/labels --inputs-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/scratch --recovered-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/recovered_candidates_v42 --out-dir work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42 | grep -E '^source_plan: stems=4 replacement_candidates=2 localized=2 unresolved=[0-9]+ before_mismatch=[0-9]+$'`\n- [ ] `for s in Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79 VISOR_S-MOC_Herbicide_91234-52-89391; do for c in pymupdf; do jq -e '.stem and .original_input_sha256 and (.operations|type)==\"array\" and (.unresolved|type)==\"array\" and .expected.final_rate_rows\u003e0' work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42/$s/line_remap_${c}_v2.json \u003e/dev/null || exit 1; done; done; jq -e '.original_input|endswith(\"Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79.v2-opus5.json\")' work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42/Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79/line_remap_pymupdf_v1.json \u003e/dev/null || exit 1; for s in Volunteer_66222-60-55467 Crop_Protect_Direct_Paraquat_3SL_101458-2; do test -f work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42/$s/plan_v2.json || exit 1; done; echo plans_ok`\n- [ ] `for s in Willowood_Metribuzin_75DF_87290-79 VISOR_S-MOC_Herbicide_91234-52-89391 Volunteer_66222-60-55467 Crop_Protect_Direct_Paraquat_3SL_101458-2; do test \"$(sha256sum /home/ben/projects/farmplanner/data/production/labels/$s/$s.md | cut -d' ' -f1)\" = \"$(jq -r .live_sha256 work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/source_repairs_v42/$s/plan_v2.json)\" || exit 1; done; echo live_sources_untouched`\n\n\n## Source review fixes\nImplement F1/F2/F3/F5/F6/F7 from artifacts/review_conversion_v42.md, in this bead. Review supplies the independent failure diagnosis; no reconversion. F1: parse actual installs/remaps/localized_repairs JSON, require passing per-stem source/remap or localized evidence, permit independently passing localized stems even when another stem fails overall; candidate none can have a verified localized replacement (original contract), so never reject that whole valid route blindly. Tests use actual review schema.\nF2/F3: ordinal numbers are not rates. Multi-line pipe tables can show a range across cells. Locate source citations by original text with normalized whitespace/fraction variants and unique content alignment; source_section often is a composite breadcrumb not a literal heading. A similarity score alone never proves a remap: require unique same-context block plus genuine amount/unit evidence, preserve uncertainties as unresolved. Record located block/pdf_page_0 and content_correction_dependency when original stored values are absent because content needs correction; do not remap them to unrelated identical numbers. Review's exact ten resolvable examples are expected outcomes; wrong VISOR soybean restrictions match must instead resolve to1167-1172/table p24. Add regressions for wrong ordinals, table extrema, composite headings and wrong old numeric values. Support genuine ⅙/⅚ and U+2044/superscript-digit fractions.\nF4 disposition: the explicit crop-section gate requires the soybean heading, so do not accept it as absent. Manager supplied exact three-line candidate_heading_repairs_v48.json. Add --candidate-repairs PATH, apply exact-before repairs to the saved candidate in memory after verifying its hash, save a VERSIONED candidate preview under out-dir/\u003cstem\u003e (never overwrite the original candidate). Plan uses that preview's path/hash; receipt retains baseline candidate hash and operations. Every word/number and line count must remain unchanged except Markdown heading prefixes and moving the existing restrictions title to the immediately preceding blank line. No converter code/run, OCR or new source text. Independent re-review will validate just those three source changes plus new remaps, reusing the passed whole-file content comparison.\nF6/F7: source_remap.py owns number/text matching/remap functions; installer owns I/O/plan/apply. New modules each under500 lines, add CODEMAP entries for installer, remap module and previously missing recovery script. Tests import owning module, no compatibility shims. F8 trailing newline accepted as a documented one-byte normalization. F9 is an expected downstream checker, not a missing current implementation; do not create it here.\nVersion all regenerated outputs: plan_v2.json, line_remap_*_v2.json, localized_preview_v2.md, corrected candidate preview_v2.md. Preserve all v1 bytes and refuse output collisions. CLI's plan may accept --version 2 for these concrete repeat outputs; Acceptance runs version2 and checks v2paths instead of v1. Never install to live labels in this builder. The output may retain genuine content-correction dependencies or ambiguity, with actionable block/page evidence, never fake unresolved=0.\n\nThe saved source_remap.py from the quota-interrupted run is559lines. Reuse it, then split concrete number/text/heading matching helpers into source_text.py if needed to keep bothmodules under500lines. Add the matching CODEMAP row; this is approved within the same source-remap responsibility split.\n\n## Second scoped source review\nRead artifacts/review_conversion_v42.v2.md. All67 emitted v2 remaps passed, both candidates and localized sources passed. Fix only G1-G4, retaining strict value/unit/unique-crop ownership. G1 number tokens must not include embedded model names such as75DF; rate columns/table rows must not pool carrier gallons, inches or partner-product amounts. Where actual values occur in a verified block but layout cannot prove their rate ownership, return values_split_across_block, not false content_correction_dependency. G2 normalize OCR/formatting only for alignment scoring, never alter values/source text or lower MATCH_FLOOR. Do not treat arbitrary percentages as fractions globally; strip markup/folio noise and normalize clearly equivalent fraction/unit representations. G3 include crop-level and local heading context so cross-crop boilerplate does not become an ambiguity or wrong match. G4 split source parsing/remap unit tests to tests/test_source_text.py; allfiles below500lines. Preserve every v1/v2 candidate/plan/remap byte, produce v3 with --version3 and same hash-bound candidate heading repairs. Existing candidate words/numbers must remain unchanged. Reuse prior wholePDF/localized reviews and existing converter/page tests. New focused regression fixtures should prove rate-column ownership and safe abstention as well as crop-heading disambiguation. Do not force unresolved counts tozero: true content dependencies and genuinely missing citations remain explicit for manager evidence. Apply-tool compatibility proof on v3 in temp only. No new conversion, extraction, GPU, live source or products writes. Version2 remains immutable even though earlier Acceptance names2; execute corresponding new-output Acceptance with3 and report both preservation and newcounts.\n","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-09-09T02:42:02.01293494+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-09T13:24:38.255950542+02:00","closed_at":"2026-09-09T13:24:38.255950542+02:00","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-09-09T02:42:02.013963346+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.10","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T02:42:44.249124637+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.9","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T02:42:51.844585328+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.5","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T02:42:55.685565863+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.33","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T08:35:37.299055259+02:00","created_by":"ben"}]