1686:{"id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.32","title":"Correct test-gate invocation and remove obsolete evidence ignore exceptions","description":"## Given/When/Then\nGiven the independently reproduced inherited-pytest-options failures and two forbidden per-item ignore rules in work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/rca_gate_v46.md, when the outer gate receives xdist arguments directly and the obsolete exceptions are removed, then all existing serial and parallel tripwire tests and repository-contract checks pass without weakening any budget.\n\n## Touches\n- `.bdc.conf`\n- `.gitignore`\n\n## Contract\nRead rca_gate_v46.md. Add -n 2 directly to the outer `uv run python -m pytest -q` command in GATE_CMD. Add one concise explanatory header sentence. Remove only the comment and two exact !/work/w893...validator...jsonl exceptions at the end of .gitignore. Both evidence files are already tracked and must remain tracked. No test changes, no budget changes, no primary writes. Do not export PYTEST_ADDOPTS. The manager handles completed builder recovery after merge.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `env -u PYTEST_ADDOPTS bdc test tests/test_duration_tripwire.py tests/test_worktree_repo_contract.py`\n- [ ] `git ls-files --error-unmatch work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/validator_runtime_impact_v45.jsonl work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/validator_actual_output_v46.jsonl`\n","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2026-09-09T07:13:58.070225561+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-09T07:16:18.596472821+02:00","closed_at":"2026-09-09T07:16:18.596472821+02:00","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.32","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-09-09T07:14:09.282499943+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.32","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T18:19:40.568401819+02:00","created_by":"ben"}]}
1687:{"id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.33","title":"Honor physical PDF page markers in citation mapping","description":"## Given/When/Then\nGiven existing marked PyMuPDF candidates and original unmarked labels, when _page_for_line resolves a citation, then physical page comments bound the heading scan and unmarked results remain byte-for-byte equivalent.\n\n## Touches\n- `farmplanner/filter/label_pages.py`\n- `tests/test_label_pages.py`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/page_recheck_v1.json`\n\n## Contract\nImplement the independently reviewed design in work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/rca_source_pages_v47.md section 1D, within plan_v48.md Citation-page repair. Exact zero-based page comments set a floor and resynchronize the TOC cursor; next explicit comment bounds the inferred page above. Old unmarked source behavior is unchanged. Existing no-TOC behavior remains. No changes to _match_page, no reconversion, no PDF/MD/candidate installation, no live writes. Test marked lag, false-forward matching, sparse-marker later progression, before-first-marker and malformed comments. The complete five-candidate and unmarked-source recheck in RCA1D is required; include last-page and adjacent-marker boundaries. Save versioned JSON evidence containing hashes, counts and all mismatches. Do not overwrite prior output.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `uv run pytest tests/test_label_pages.py tests/test_rate_caveat.py tests/test_convert_label_textlayer.py -q`\n- [ ] `python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/artifacts/conversion_v42/page_recheck_v1.json')); assert d['candidate_count']==5 and d['candidate_mismatches']==0 and d['unmarked_differences']==0 and d['localized_wrong_sites']==0; print('five_label_page_recheck_pass')\"`\n","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2026-09-09T08:35:33.349057234+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-09T08:44:42.093857932+02:00","closed_at":"2026-09-09T08:44:42.093857932+02:00","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.33","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T08:35:33.496029199+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.33","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-09-09T18:19:40.766939811+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.33","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.32","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T18:19:40.791890267+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.33","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.20","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T18:19:40.816026317+02:00","created_by":"ben"}]}
1688:{"id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.34","title":"Enforce reviewed citation maps and recoverable source installation before live writes","description":"## Given/When/Then\n**Given:** plan_v49.md, source review artifacts/review_conversion_v42.v4.md PASS, complete reviewed maps of69 Willowood and79 VISOR rows, plus two reviewed zero-shift localized previews; current apply is a proposal-stage stub.\n**When:** the reviewed source installation CLI and live citation checker run against temporary label fixtures.\n**Then:** only the exact reviewed bytes can install, all refusal checks precede a live write, each write is recoverable and recorded, and the checker proves installed source and runtime pages. This bead implements and tests tooling only. No real label or products writes.\n\n## Touches\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/source_install.py`\n- `work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/verify/textlayer_sites_check.py`\n- `tests/test_install_label_sources.py`\n- `tests/test_source_installation.py`\n- `tests/test_textlayer_sites_check.py`\n- `CODEMAP.md`\n- `codemap/testing.md`\n\n## Contract\n- Read plan_v49 section Reviewed citation maps are the installation boundary, the existing bead8.16 contract for receipt/checker semantics, and review_conversion_v42.v4.md. Do not rewrite source_remap.py or source_text.py and do not repeat conversion, PDF inventory, model judgments or extraction. Keep all prior artifacts unchanged. No prompt edits.\n- Preserve the plan CLI. Replace unsafe apply implementation, moving installation responsibility into source_install.py if needed. Every affected Python file must finish below500 lines; split existing apply tests into the named new test module rather than adding to440line file. Migrate imports/callers, no compatibility shims.\n- Actual apply interface remains per stem: apply --stem NAME --plan-dir DIR --review REPORT --labels-dir DIR --parked-dir DIR --version3 [--apply]. Read plan_v3.json. Parse the existing fenced Markdown review with review_bindings.verdict_json; no raw-JSON fallback.\n- Replacement install authority is review.remaps[stem].path+sha256. Read that exact map and require its hash, passing verdict, chosen candidate path/hash and all source bindings, original input hash, unresolved empty, unique signatures and complete coverage of canonical FIRST-kept dedup rows. Every before must equal the complete canonical row; only source_line_range may differ. Confirm each new range is within the reviewed candidate and its page marker equals pdf_page_0. Use existing pure correction/dedup mechanisms where useful. Never rerun the heuristic locator or merge unreviewed proposals during apply. Reject missing digest, changed bytes, incomplete coverage, wrong before, mismatched source/candidate/input, rejected signatures, or non-pass review before writes.\n- Localized authority is review.localized_repairs[stem].remap_path plus preview_sha256 and the matching plan candidate. Current two maps have0ops, no line shifts: validate no operations, original hash, unchanged canonical rows and preview exact changed lines against the already reviewed localized_repairs_proposal_v2.json. Current review v4 reuses prior review and binds preview SHA; it does not contain a localized map digest. Do not invent a reviewer digest: structural zero-operation validation plus exact reviewed preview is sufficient. Refuse any nonzero localized map in this item. Known line edits and page comments are in the existing proposal. No regenerated previews.\n- For both routes, live source SHA must still equal plan.live_sha256 and, where present, review.baseline_sources[stem].sha256. Validate actual PDF/source hashes. Dry-run performs the same preflight and creates NO directories/files.\n- Apply one stem at a time: preflight output collisions; exclusive new parked original \u003cparked-dir\u003e/\u003cstem\u003e.ocr.md (a fresh version only if caller explicitly selects it, otherwise refuse collision); same-directory exclusive .md.bak.\u003cUTC\u003e, verify both against old SHA; same-target hash recheck immediately before atomic replace. Preserve permissions. Verify installed bytes against reviewed candidate SHA; restore old bytes atomically and verify on any post-write failure. Never write PDF/_meta.json or products. No rm/unlink cleanup of user files; scratch files can be banked via approved trash mechanism. Any partial durable artifact must fail closed for retry, never authorize a second write.\n- Produce plan-dir/\u003cstem\u003e/line_remap_v1.json byte-identical to the reviewed final map (localized identical validated empty map) and receipt_v1.json with stem,kind,candidate,review_path,review_sha256,old_sha256,new_sha256,parked_path,backup_path,applied:true, remap:{operations,manual,unresolved:0}, and reviewed_map_path/sha256 plus installed final_map hash. Use repository-relative artifact paths for durability across run merge, absolute only for real external live/backup paths. Refuse existing canonical outputs before touching live; retain old versions.\n- Checker CLI: verify/textlayer_sites_check.py --labels-dir DIR --parked-dir DIR --comparison JSON --review REPORT --plan-dir DIR. Read canonical receipts/maps and review, verify live/review/candidate/map/parked/backup hashes. For every replacement operation, exercise the real runtime page mapping at its new start and require pdf_page_0+1. The public page_for_line function has no labels-dir argument: use the actual label store/config boundary correctly, never invent a signature. Also check comparison known_sites needles and section_boundaries headings occur once; inspect actual comparison shape. Check localized changed lines and page markers too. Print conversion_pdf_pass=2/2 only when both replacements AND all required localized checks pass; nonzero on any defect. No receipt-only fabricated pass.\n- Tests must exercise real temp CLI/record data shape and atomic refusal/rollback paths: altered reviewed digest/map, wrong first-before, omitted/duplicate row, changed live/candidate/PDF/input, dry-run no writes, collision no overwrite, write failure restoration, successful replacement and localized write, runtime page failure and missing known site. Use5 representative existing label shapes for the transformation validation where applicable, reuse earlier approved full-PDF evidence rather than auditing them again. Avoid implementation-mirroring assertions.\n- Code-only builder: no primary writes and no source receipts in actual data_runs. Manager will independently review this commit before bead8.16 executes it. Report includes exact code/test changes and tests; normal bdc full gate required. Do not stop merely because review notes require later execution.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `uv run python -m pytest -q tests/test_install_label_sources.py tests/test_source_installation.py tests/test_textlayer_sites_check.py`\n- [ ] `uv run python work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py apply --help | grep -q -- --apply`\n- [ ] `uv run python work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/verify/textlayer_sites_check.py --help | grep -q -- --labels-dir`\n- [ ] `python3 -c \"from pathlib import Path; ps=[Path(p) for p in ('work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py','work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/source_install.py','work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/verify/textlayer_sites_check.py','tests/test_install_label_sources.py','tests/test_source_installation.py','tests/test_textlayer_sites_check.py')]; assert all(len(p.read_text().splitlines())\u003c500 for p in ps if p.exists()); print('size_gate=pass')\"`\n","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:23:45.98977019+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-09T15:08:35.317374905+02:00","closed_at":"2026-09-09T15:08:35.317374905+02:00","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.34","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:23:45.9984512+02:00","created_by":"ben"},{"issue_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.34","depends_on_id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.31","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:23:46.116555896+02:00","created_by":"ben"}]}

