lects it, otherwise refuse collision); same-directory exclusive .md.bak.\u003cUTC\u003e, verify both against old SHA; same-target hash recheck immediately before atomic replace. Preserve permissions. Verify installed bytes against reviewed candidate SHA; restore old bytes atomically and verify on any post-write failure. Never write PDF/_meta.json or products. No rm/unlink cleanup of user files; scratch files can be banked via approved trash mechanism. Any partial durable artifact must fail closed for retry, never authorize a second write.\n- Produce plan-dir/\u003cstem\u003e/line_remap_v1.json byte-identical to the reviewed final map (localized identical validated empty map) and receipt_v1.json with stem,kind,candidate,review_path,review_sha256,old_sha256,new_sha256,parked_path,backup_path,applied:true, remap:{operations,manual,unresolved:0}, and reviewed_map_path/sha256 plus installed final_map hash. Use repository-relative artifact paths for durability across run merge, absolute only for real external live/backup paths. Refuse existing canonical outputs before touching live; retain old versions.\n- Checker CLI: verify/textlayer_sites_check.py --labels-dir DIR --parked-dir DIR --comparison JSON --review REPORT --plan-dir DIR. Read canonical receipts/maps and review, verify live/review/candidate/map/parked/backup hashes. For every replacement operation, exercise the real runtime page mapping at its new start and require pdf_page_0+1. The public page_for_line function has no labels-dir argument: use the actual label store/config boundary correctly, never invent a signature. Also check comparison known_sites needles and section_boundaries headings occur once; inspect actual comparison shape. Check localized changed lines and page markers too. Print conversion_pdf_pass=2/2 only when both replacements AND all required localized checks pass; nonzero on any defect. No receipt-only fabricated pass.\n- Tests must exercise real temp CLI/record data shape and atomic refusal/rollback paths: altered reviewed digest/map, wrong first-before, omitted/duplicate row, changed live/candidate/PDF/input, dry-run no writes, collision no overwrite, write failure restoration, successful replacement and localized write, runtime page failure and missing known site. Use5 representative existing label shapes for the transformation validation where applicable, reuse earlier approved full-PDF evidence rather than auditing them again. Avoid implementation-mirroring assertions.\n- Code-only builder: no primary writes and no source receipts in actual data_runs. Manager will independently review this commit before bead8.16 executes it. Report includes exact code/test changes and tests; normal bdc full gate required. Do not stop merely because review notes require later execution.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `uv run python -m pytest -q tests/test_install_label_sources.py tests/test_source_installation.py tests/test_textlayer_sites_check.py`\n- [ ] `uv run python work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py apply --help | grep -q -- --apply`\n- [ ] `uv run python work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/verify/textlayer_sites_check.py --help | grep -q -- --labels-dir`\n- [ ] `python3 -c \"from pathlib import Path; ps=[Path(p) for p in ('work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/install_label_sources.py','work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/source_install.py','work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/verify/textlayer_sites_check.py','tests/test_install_label_sources.py','tests/test_source_installation.py','tests/test_textlayer_sites_check.py')]; assert all(len(p.read_text().splitlines())\u003c500 for p in ps if p.exists()); print('size_gate=pass')\"`\n","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:23:45.98977019+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-09T14:51:00.076753016+02:00","closed_at":"2026-09-09T14:51:00.076753016+02:00","close_reason":"Closed"}|{"close_reason":"","closed_at":null,"status":"in_progress"}||2026-09-09 13:02:37
