14893|farmplanner-r3yq.8.32|created|ben||{"id":"farmplanner-r3yq.8.32","title":"Validate rate-dependency crops against the canonical crop vocabulary, not labeled_crops","description":"## Given/When/Then\n**Given:** `scripts/promote_rates.py` `validate_products_against_base` refuses any `rate_dependencies[i].affected_crops` value that is not in the product's `labeled_crops` (the loop after `labeled_crop_names(staged_product)`, message `... not in labeled_crops`). The extraction prompt (`farmplanner/data/prompts/extraction_rates.txt`, \"Rate-dependent rotation\") defines a RateDependency's `affected_crops` as the crops whose plantback interval the rate changes: rotational crops, which are often not labeled uses. The runtime (`farmplanner/filter/candidates.py` `_compact_dep`) only renders them as text. The batch-1 promotion (`artifacts/rates_promotion_v42_batch1.md`) held VISOR_S-MOC_89167-40-89391 on this rule for a PDF-verified `rotation_interval` over alfalfa, barley, clover, oats, rye and wheat, and the corpus already carries three such dependencies counted as pre-existing base issues (Diuron_80_WDG winter wheat, Goal_2XL twice).\n**When:** the dependency crop check validates each `affected_crops` value against the canonical crop vocabulary (`farmplanner.data.loaders.load_target_crops()`, the same list the schema applies to `labeled_crops.crop` and `rotation.crop`) instead of the product's labeled crops.\n**Then:** a rotational crop that is a canonical name passes; a name outside the vocabulary (for example `rye`, whose canonical name is `cereal rye`) still fails with a message naming the value and `not a canonical crop`; `application_rates[i].crops` keep the existing labeled-crops rule unchanged; `validate` on the live file still prints PASS and its `base_preexisting_issues` drops by exactly the three corpus dependencies named above (49 to 46 on the current live file) and by nothing else.\n## Touches\n- `scripts/promote_rates.py`\n- `tests/test_promote_rates.py`\n- `codemap/scripts-data-build.md`\n## Contract\n- Change only the dependency loop's membership set and message; load the vocabulary once per validation run, not per product; no change to `labeled_crop_names`, the rates-row crop rule, cap rules, snapshot or `_reviews` logic.\n- Tests: rewrite the existing assertion `assert \"not in labeled_crops\" in str(excinfo.value)` in `test_unscoped_assemble_still_raises_on_base_error` only if that fixture's failure comes from a dependency crop (if it comes from a rates-row crop, leave it); add one test where a dependency names a canonical crop absent from `labeled_crops` and validation passes, and one where it names a non-vocabulary word and validation fails with the new message. Fixtures must not read the production vocabulary file: monkeypatch the loader.\n- Update the `scripts/promote_rates.py` row in `codemap/scripts-data-build.md` with the vocabulary rule in the same commit.\n- No live data write. The VISOR promotion is bead farmplanner-r3yq.8.36.\n## Acceptance\n- Run every command below from the root of the current run checkout (the builder's worktree), never a hard-coded item checkout; absolute `/home/ben/projects/farmplanner/...` paths name authorized live data only.\n- [ ] `uv run pytest tests/test_promote_rates.py -q -k \"dependency or canonical or base_error\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1 | grep -qE '^[0-9]+ passed'`\n- [ ] `uv run python scripts/promote_rates.py validate --products /home/ben/projects/farmplanner/data/production/products.json --manifest work/w893_edition-dedup-copy/data_runs/rates_manifest_v42_batch1.json | grep -qE '^PASS validate .* base_preexisting_issues=46$'`\n- [ ] `! grep -n 'not in labeled_crops' scripts/promote_rates.py | grep -q 'rate_dependencies' \u0026\u0026 grep -q 'not a canonical crop' scripts/promote_rates.py`\n","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2026-09-09T18:19:40.566936372+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-09T18:19:40.566936372+02:00"}||2026-09-09 16:19:40
