# Transcript Search

One tool searches all agent transcripts on this host: `~/projects/shared-docs/skills/transcript-search/mine-transcripts.py`.

| `--root` | Corpus |
|----------|--------|
| `default`, `-s`, `-x`, `-y`, `-z`, `-glm` | Claude variants: `~/.claude*/projects/`, including `subagents/**` workers |
| `codex` | `~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl` |
| `openclaw` | `~/.openclaw/agents/*/sessions/*.jsonl` |
| `opencode` | `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` (`session`/`message`/`part` tables, read-only) |

Subcommands: `search` (regex/literal), `sessions` (recent + first prompts), `corrections` (human pushback, interactive sessions only), `errors` (Claude-only signal; other root labels exit 2). No args = roots dashboard.

## Search

```bash
M=~/projects/shared-docs/skills/transcript-search/mine-transcripts.py     # absolute: works from any cwd
python3 $M search "wt-merge exit 3"                      # all ecosystems, last 30d
python3 $M search "ENOSPC" --role error --days 90
python3 $M search "Write review to" --root codex --kind dispatched --limit 5
python3 $M search "caddy reload" --project shared-docs
python3 $M search "old phrase" --days 9999               # all time: minutes, not seconds
```

- `--kind interactive|dispatched|subagent`: human at the keyboard | headless (`claude -p`/SDK, `codex exec`, heartbeat) | spawned workers (`subagents/**`, `agent-*.jsonl`, Codex thread-spawn). Every row shows its kind; `[unknown]` = markers missing, never silently dropped.
- Leading-dash labels need the `=` form: `--root=-s`. An invalid label exits 2.
- `--project` matches Claude project dirs and Codex header cwd. OpenClaw is project-unscoped: skipped under `--project`, with a note printing the exact rerun command.
- Codex searches append `history hits outside window` from `~/.codex/history.jsonl` — user-typed prompts only, all time, not full coverage.
- Zero hits with the right roots and window IS the answer. Output caps at `--limit` (default 50) — raise it when counting, or the count is a floor.

## Read a found session

Conversation only — user/assistant text, no tool activity:

```bash
~/projects/shared-docs/skills/transcript-search/clean-transcript.sh <file>        # Claude
~/projects/shared-docs/skills/transcript-search/clean-codex-transcript.sh <file>  # Codex
```

OpenCode (`<session-id>` or `opencode:<session-id>`, from a search hit row):

```bash
~/projects/shared-docs/skills/transcript-search/clean-opencode-transcript.sh <session-id>
```

OpenClaw (handles string and text-block-list content):

```bash
jq -r 'select(.type=="message") | .message | select(.role=="user" or .role=="assistant")
  | .role + ": " + (if (.content|type)=="string" then .content
    else ([.content[]? | select(.type=="text") | .text] | join("\n")) end)' <file>
```

Tool-role hit? Pull the raw events the renderers omit:

```bash
# Claude: tool_use blocks
jq -c 'select(.message.content? | type == "array") | .message.content[]? | select(.type == "tool_use")' <file>
# Codex: function/custom tool calls
jq -c 'select(.type == "response_item" and (.payload.type == "function_call" or .payload.type == "custom_tool_call")) | .payload' <file>
# OpenClaw: toolCall items
jq -c 'select(.type == "message") | .message.content? | select(type == "array")[]? | select(.type == "toolCall")' <file>
```

## Resume a found session

| Hit | Resume |
|-----|--------|
| Claude `<sessionId>.jsonl` | sessionId = basename; cwd = decoded slug or any line's `cwd` field; launcher = the variant dir (`~/.claude-x` → `claude-x`) |
| Claude `agent-*.jsonl` | Not directly resumable — resume the parent sessionId, the path component above `subagents/` |
| `-glm` root | Read-only: headless-only lane, never launch interactively |
| `codex` | id = rollout filename tail; `codex resume <id>` is version-dependent — check `codex resume --help` first |
